<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahurutshe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hurutshe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bahurutshe are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana people</a> regarded in tradition as the senior line from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakwena">Bakwena</a> and other Tswana groups branched. By the 16th century they lived in the Marico area of the western highveld, where their stone-walled capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaditshwene">Kaditshwene</a> was one of the largest towns in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1820. Scattered in the wars of the 1820s, they regrouped and today live around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeerust">Zeerust</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>.</p></div>
